   "$comment": [
+    "0.2.35 (2026-10-11, P296): from Vahid's reads R and L of 2026-10-11, each printed with the country selected when it ran (docs/run-a/p294-reads.md). grade: its list after gradingSystemId = 6, read with 'Not in list' as the institution and Iran as the country, recorded as listsAfter with under: institution-ts-control = 'Not in list', institutionCountry-ts-control = IRAN — R's own under: the values as R printed them, the names those of the boxes that set the selects R printed (frontedBy), as docs/run-a/p294-reads.md says (docs/captures/sheffield-pgt-2026-09-10/reads/p294-R-grade-after-institution-escape-gpa20.json); the 203 entries are R's values in R's order, less its first line, 'Select your grade...', which is the list's prompt and is now recorded as such so it is never offered as an answer. Every line R printed was already among the field's options. These reads replace neither record of the country entered by hand in P294 (0.2.34 said the reads planned next would): R prints the grading system's value, 6, not its list after the escape, and T searched 'azad' and 'sheff', not 'HHE'. Both records still rest on his words of 2026-10-10 (docs/run-a/p295-his-message-as-sent.txt): \"I confirm that my reads of 6 October were made with the country set to Iran.\" unlistedInstitution and unlistedDegree: labelled from L (docs/captures/sheffield-pgt-2026-09-10/reads/p294-L-escape-box-labels.json), which printed no label, aria-label, placeholder or title for any of the three boxes, and each row's text. No labelSource is claimed: the observer did not read these labels; L, a console read, printed the row's text. unlistedDegree's row text is one sentence and is the label, normalised as the observer normalises row text (whitespace collapsed, ends trimmed). unlistedInstitution's row text is three sentences, two of help and one addressed to the box; the label is the third, cut at the row's last sentence boundary and otherwise unchanged. That is a judgement made in P296. The observer would not have made it: it gives a control no label from its own words when they run to more than one sentence or end as a statement (apps/browser-runner/src/observe-script.ts), and this sentence ends with a full stop. unlistedSubject's existing label is L's row text under the same normalisation, unchanged.",
     "0.2.34 (2026-10-09, P294): two of Vahid's reads carry the country they were made under, under: institutionCountry-ts-control = IRAN — institution-ts-control's 'HHE' search and gradingSystemId's list after 'Not in list' as the institution — at his word: \"Record the country a read was made under in the reads record itself, and make the check refuse a mapping row whose key does not match the country of the read it rests on.\" These two reads did not print the country. IRAN was entered by hand in P294 from what states it beside them: the reads file (docs/captures/sheffield-pgt-2026-09-10/reads/p291-six-reads-as-sent.txt) heads read 1 '1 — UNTOUCHED (country Iran only)', and the plan the reads followed (docs/run-a/p290-reads.md) asks for Iran as the country; 'Iran' is the label of the country box's entry IRAN. The reads planned next print the country with each list (docs/run-a/p294-reads.md) and replace this record. The subject's searches carry none: its list follows the search box only.",
     "0.2.26 (2026-09-16, P153): four label fixes before Vahid signs, at his word ('If the labels in the blueprint are wrong, then the thing I read and the thing I signed are not the same thing'). (1) The nationality page's radios carry the option labels the third read found (2026-09-14) — Yes / No, and the document-status sentences — where the third read's values equal this draft's; P110's rewrite of the values from the markup had set every option label to the field's own name. Restored: livedOutsideCountry, alwaysUKResident, alwaysEUResident, refugeeStatus, migrantWorker, spouseOfUKCitizen, euPassport, spouseOfEUCitizen, previousStudentVisa, passportScanStatus, visaScanStatus, utilityBillScanStatus, proofOfUKSpouseStatus, refugeeProofStatus. Not restored, because the third read's 'no' label ran on into the row's help text: britishPassport, indefinateVisa, livingInUK — they keep the field's name and are off a resident abroad's path. (2) dobMonth and dobYear carry 'Date of Birth:*', startYear 'Start Date:*' and endYear 'End Date:' — the row's question, which the read attached to the row's first control (dobDay, startMonth, endMonth); the same one-row-several-controls shape P131 recorded for the markers, now in the labels. No labelSource is claimed for the carried ones: the row was read, the sibling was not. (3) institutionCountry and institutionCode carry frontedBy — the Tom Select boxes that set them — so the plan lists them nowhere; they were read as 'left empty' when the boxes fill them. The thirteen unread labels of the five-pages read (fundingNationality, countryOfBirth, permanentResidence, yearsOnStudentVisa, monthsOnStudentVisa, applicationLocation, …) and 'grade' still carry the field's name: no capture holds their question, and a label the file did not carry is not invented.",
     "0.2.25 (2026-09-16, P150): the country box (institutionCountry-ts-control) carries the row's question as its label — 'Select the country the institution is based in:' — the text the third read found on the row and attached to the hidden <select id=\"institutionCountry\"> the box fronts (0.2.18, P126). The box and the select share one row; the preview shows the box, and a student reading 'institutionCountry-ts-control: United Kingdom' at the yes would be reading a DOM id. No labelSource is claimed: the read labelled the select, not the box.",
